e a projection argument (program attributes for merge requests, cluster attributes here) so both are one three-way with two projections. Proofs, a table on values with d/with targets: this test (main pulls the end, the refined intent and a child task by eid); a-value-changed-on-both-sides-resolves-by-the-declared-rule (table over :root, :theirs, :add; under :root the entity's other attribute still copies); program-and-runtime-facts-never-copy (a defn, an evaluation, a turn and a received message yield empty tx-data); a-copy-of-an-unchanged-branch-is-empty; a-retraction-on-the-branch-retracts-on-an-unchanged-main-only; a-branch-born-entity-keeps-its-eid-on-main (the child task's eid on main equals its eid on the branch, refs included; main's next allocation is unmoved); a-natural-identity-born-on-both-sides-maps-to-mains-eid (two branches each mint an occurrence with one signature: main holds one entity under its own eid, count summed by :add, every ref remapped); the-merge-base-is-the-merge-requests (the squash's base commit equals `seon.cluster.source/merge-base` for the same branch); cost row: a ten-evaluation attempt under 10 ms / 5 MB through seon.profile/measure. Files: src/seon/cluster/squash.clj, test/seon/cluster/squash_test.clj, src/seon/cluster/source.clj (merge-base public), src/seon/program.cljc (projection argument)."
